{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Zakharov's theorem that, for every base g >= 2, the set of natural numbers that are a sum of two base-g palindromes has lower (indeed natural) density zero; this answers Problem 95 of Ben Green's list of 100 open problems in the negative. Two statements of the formal-conjectures file GreensOpenProblems/95.lean are proved: Green95.green_95 (the set of sums of two base-g palindromes, 0 allowed, does not have positive lower density) and Green95.green_95.variants.zakharov (for every g >= 2 there is c > 0 such that, for all large X, the number of n < X that are a sum of two positive base-g palindromes is at most X / (log X)^c). The development proves an explicit exponent c = 1/10 and the density statements for the upper, lower and natural density. The proof uses only the standard axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.",
